Z||000000||gtsonly||09-02-2000||12:47 AM||||Lets just say, one day your driving along and in a semi-darkened parking lot you see a group of rice-runners discussing who has the biggest exhaust tip on their $500.00 honda civic. Being a proud Fiero owner you want to show the pre-pubesent import jockey's (also your wife, significant other or life partner who may or may not be in the car telling you to act your age) the power of the Fiero by whipping into a wicked doughnut!! Mind you this is a "on the spot burst of testosterone" and not recommended as a daily maneuver. With all fun said, how do you or can you prevent the nasty front end push Fiero's seem to have?? Camber adjustments? Mine is a bone stock 86 GT. <BR>  Chris Hatch<BR>  1986.5 GT with T-Tops||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||09-02-2000||10:09 AM||||Lower suspension, poly bushings, bigger wider tires, or a V-8 in the back!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||09-02-2000||01:24 PM||||Ummmm...<BR>Add rear stabilizer bar?<BR>Wait for snow?  That would help...  <P>Wait - ! If you know ahead of time which direction you want the back end to go, you can steer the rear by adjusting the rear toe links  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ! <P>Warning: don't try this at home !  Especially, not with <B>my</B> car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !||||reg||12
Z||000003||Tryxalon||09-02-2000||08:43 PM||||Well, IF you just Gotta "showoff!" rather than the "do-nut", why not use the characteristics of your car (specifically that "oh so terrible" 'trailing throttle oversteer' with a little bit of 'heel and toe') and show them what a 'bootlegger turn' is. (a 180) <P>Bettcha THEY can't duplicate it, but your suspension makes it easy!! (practice in a secluded vacant lot a few times, first ... just to learn the limits of your car - you can 'over-rotate'!!) <P>One word of caution: This can cause excessive tire wear and possibly require more often rear wheel alignment. <P>||||reg||6
Z||000004||Sillhouette.com||09-02-2000||09:11 PM||||Here is what I do.  <BR>Speed towards your intended area of play in second gear.  Downshift into first and pop I mean pop the clutch while starting the turn.  The car will go into a wild spin as the tires lock up.  Also the sudden decelartion shifts the weight of the car to the front so no more push on your Fiero.  Now this was done on a lowered car with KYB all around 16" tires and poly bushings.  <P><BR>Later||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||09-02-2000||09:27 PM||||This topic reminds me off all the fun we used to have doing backwards donuts in the old VW Rabbit diesel truck. Empty grass field, full lock steering, reverse and open it up! It also works with other front drive cars- the g-force is unreal!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||09-02-2000||09:59 PM||||Ahhhh, backwards donuts.  Now those are fun!  Try a few in a snowy parking lot in an 86 Olds Delta 88 with the 3.8 litre V6.  muhahahahahaha  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000007||gtsonly||09-04-2000||07:15 AM||||for all those reading, kmow that i would never do dounuts or otherwise "rag" on my car. the story prior to my question was just an "ice breaker" joking about a funny situation with a serious question. on a side note, back in high school years and years ago, i use to use my fathers front wheel drive olds fieasta( i think thats how you spell it) to do the old starsky and hutch reverse skid and throw it into forward all while spinning 180 degrees. i keep kids amuzed for hours!! try that in a fiero!!!<P>   chris hatch||||reg||6
Z||000008||Carrolles||09-05-2000||09:40 AM||||A rear swaybar did wonders for the handling on my 85SE v-6 4spd.  I used an Addco that I got from JC Whitney.<P>Suspension is otherwise stock.||||reg||1
